.venv/
scratch/
dist/
__pycache__/
data/*
data/PSF/*
examples/*fits
examples/stars/
examples/*
!examples/verify_pipeline.ipynb
!examples/run_*.py
!examples/*.json
!examples/make_minerva_configs.py
# MINERVA runs are working data, not part of the package: the configs are
# generated by examples/make_minerva_configs.py (which IS tracked) and
# everything else in there is run output. Ignore the tree wholesale.
examples/minerva/
# CANFAR and OzStar toolkits: tracked in full. These directories are staging
# only - launch scripts, docs, and the generated per-band configs and staging
# lists - and they stay lightweight (all text, under a megabyte). Outputs must
# never be written here; submit.py sends fetched results and upload scratch to
# scratch/<toolkit>/, which is gitignored. The configs do carry a hardcoded
# username and run root, which is the price of having the exact inputs of a
# campaign in the history.
#
# `examples/*` above stops git descending into a directory at all, so the two
# have to be un-ignored before any rule inside them can apply.
# Campaign toolkits: track the scripts and docs, never the generated configs.
# arcify.py/ozify.py rewrite a MINERVA config into <name>_canfar.json or
# <name>_ozstar.json with absolute paths for one cluster and one account -
# /fred/<project>/<user>/... and /arc/... - so they are per-machine working
# data, not source. Regenerate them; do not commit them.
!examples/canfar/
!examples/ozstar/
examples/canfar/*
examples/ozstar/*
!examples/canfar/*.py
!examples/canfar/*.md
!examples/canfar/*.sh
!examples/ozstar/*.py
!examples/ozstar/*.md
!examples/ozstar/*.sh
!examples/canfar/jobs/
examples/canfar/jobs/*
!examples/canfar/jobs/*.sh
# .py as well as .sh: a job whose logic does not fit in shell ships its script
# alongside the wrapper, and `submit.py push` uploads jobs/*.py for exactly
# that. The OzStar block below already allows them.
!examples/canfar/jobs/*.py
!examples/ozstar/jobs/
examples/ozstar/jobs/*
!examples/ozstar/jobs/*.sh
!examples/ozstar/jobs/*.slurm
!examples/ozstar/jobs/*.py

# The remote-access toolkit: shell helpers that fetch a CADC proxy certificate
# and mount /arc over sshfs. Tracked, because getting a new machine onto CANFAR
# is part of running a campaign and the alternative is a page of prose. Its
# `canfar.conf` is not: it names one CADC account, so the account-free
# `canfar.conf.example` is what ships and the working copy stays out.
!examples/canfar/remote/
examples/canfar/remote/*
!examples/canfar/remote/*.sh
!examples/canfar/remote/*.example
legacy/autopilot/*png
legacy/autopilot/*pdf
# IDL reference-run output: 2.4 MB of FITS per run, regenerable from the
# .pro sources next to it. Binaries do not come out of git history again.
legacy/subphot/example_output/
!data/*test*
!data/PSF/
!data/PSF/*OS4_GRID25*
!data/PSF/*OS4_GRID9*
!data/examples/*ipynb
!data/examples/*py
.DS_Store
.claude/
.codex/
.serena/
.mcp.json

# Sphinx build output
docs/_build/
docs/api/
